# PAM policy for shoestring-lock (the screen locker) — Linux / Linux-PAM.
#
# A dedicated stack, NOT the system `login` service, so the locker verifies
# the *current* user's password directly and inherits no login-time policy
# surprises. `pam_unix` transparently uses the setuid `unix_chkpwd` helper
# (shipped in libpam-modules / pam) so an unprivileged locker can check the
# password without the binary itself being setuid.
auth     required  pam_unix.so
account  required  pam_unix.so
